---
import cairnMarkRaw from '../../../assets/images/cairn/cairn.svg?raw';

const meta_title = 'Cairn Privacy Policy';
const meta_description = 'Privacy policy for Cairn, a body-measurement tracker for Android & Wear OS. Cairn makes no network calls — everything stays in Health Connect, on your device.';
const canonicalUrl = 'https://clivewalkden.co.uk/apps/cairn/privacy/';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl}>
    <meta name="description" content={meta_description}>
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl}>
    <meta property="og:title" content={meta_title}>
    <meta property="og:description" content={meta_description}>
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Cairn">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={meta_title}>
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={meta_description}>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico">
    <title>{meta_title}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500;9..144,600&family=Nunito+Sans:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
      :root {
        --cream: #FAF6F0;
        --ink: #3A2E27;
        --ink-soft: #6b5d53;
        --terracotta: #C97C5D;
        --terracotta-deep: #a85f42;
        --sage: #8CA394;
        --sand: #E8C9A0;
        --rule: #e4d7c6;
        --card: #ffffff;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
          --cream: #2A2521;
          --ink: #F0E6DC;
          --ink-soft: #cbbfb4;
          --terracotta: #d99677;
          --terracotta-deep: #e8b299;
          --sage: #a3bcac;
          --sand: #6b5a42;
          --rule: #423a33;
          --card: #332c27;
        }
      }
      :root[data-theme="dark"] {
        --cream: #2A2521;
        --ink: #F0E6DC;
        --ink-soft: #cbbfb4;
        --terracotta: #d99677;
        --terracotta-deep: #e8b299;
        --sage: #a3bcac;
        --sand: #6b5a42;
        --rule: #423a33;
        --card: #332c27;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
      body {
        background: var(--cream);
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: 'Nunito Sans', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.65;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      img { max-width: 100%; }
      h1, h2 {
        font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
        font-optical-sizing: auto;
        color: var(--ink);
        text-wrap: balance;
      }

      .page {
        max-width: 680px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 64px 24px 96px;
      }

      /* Masthead: the app's own icon mark */
      .masthead { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
      .mark { width: 46px; height: 46px; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .mark svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }

      .wordmark { font-family: 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2px; }
      .tagline { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 14.5px; margin-top: 2px; }

      .updated {
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 13px;
        margin-top: 22px;
        padding-top: 18px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }

      .lede {
        font-size: 18px;
        margin-top: 34px;
        color: var(--ink);
      }
      .lede strong { color: var(--terracotta-deep); font-weight: 700; }

      section { margin-top: 44px; }
      section h2 {
        font-size: 21px;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin: 0 0 14px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: baseline;
        gap: 10px;
      }
      section h2::before {
        content: '';
        width: 7px; height: 7px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--sage);
        display: inline-block;
        transform: translateY(-2px);
      }
      section p { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--ink); }
      section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
      section ul { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 22px; }
      section li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
      section li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

      code, .rt {
        font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        font-size: 0.9em;
        background: var(--sand);
        color: var(--ink);
        padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
        border-radius: 4px;
      }
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) code, :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .rt { color: var(--ink); }

      /* Data-flow reference table — the one structural device that earns its place here: every
         record type this app can touch, mapped to whether Cairn writes it and where it can go. */
      .flow-table {
        margin-top: 16px;
        border: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-radius: 10px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: var(--card);
      }
      .flow-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 0.85fr 0.75fr;
        gap: 10px;
        padding: 12px 16px;
        align-items: center;
      }
      .flow-row + .flow-row { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .flow-head {
        font-size: 11.5px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        background: transparent;
      }
      .flow-row .rtype { font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 13px; }
      .pill {
        display: inline-block;
        font-size: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
        padding: 3px 10px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      .pill.write { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--terracotta) 22%, transparent); color: var(--terracotta-deep); }
      .pill.read  { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sage) 28%, transparent); color: var(--ink); }
      .pill.no    { background: transparent; color: var(--ink-soft); }

      .callout {
        margin-top: 16px;
        padding: 16px 18px;
        background: var(--card);
        border-left: 3px solid var(--sage);
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-size: 15px;
      }
      .callout p { margin: 0; }

      footer {
        margin-top: 56px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
        font-size: 14px;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }
      footer a { color: var(--terracotta-deep); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; }
      footer a:hover { opacity: 0.75; }

      @media (max-width: 480px) {
        .flow-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page">

      <div class="masthead">
        <div class="mark" set:html={cairnMarkRaw} />
        <div>
          <div class="wordmark">Cairn</div>
          <div class="tagline">Body-measurement tracker for Android &amp; Wear OS</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h1 style="font-size: 32px; margin: 30px 0 0;">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="updated">Last updated 6 September 2026</div>

      <p class="lede">
        Cairn has <strong>no account, no analytics, and makes no network calls of any kind.</strong> Everything
        it reads or writes lives in <strong>Android Health Connect</strong>, on your device,
        under your control. Nothing about you or your health ever reaches us, because there's no
        server for it to reach.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>What Cairn stores</h2>
        <p>Only when you log or edit an entry yourself &mdash; from the phone app or the watch quick-log:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Weight, height, body fat %, and body water (stored as a derived mass)</li>
          <li>Heart rate, if you turn on continuous monitoring on the watch &mdash; delivered by
            Wear OS's own Health Services in the background, in small batches, and off again the
            moment you disable it from the watch app's home screen</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Deleting an entry in Cairn deletes the matching Health Connect records with it. Nothing
          is retained anywhere else &mdash; there is nowhere else.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What Cairn reads</h2>
        <p>The fields above, to keep its own copy in sync with Health Connect, plus a handful of
          figures it displays for context but never writes itself: steps, active and total calories,
          exercise sessions and distance, and sleep sessions. Sleep in particular is never captured
          by Cairn &mdash; it's read from whatever your watch's own software already recorded.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Where each record type goes</h2>
        <p>A record-by-record account, since "your data" means different things depending which
          figure you mean:</p>
        <div class="flow-table">
          <div class="flow-row flow-head">
            <div>Health Connect record</div>
            <div>Cairn's role</div>
            <div>Leaves this device?</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">WeightRecord</div><div><span class="pill write">Writes</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">HeightRecord</div><div><span class="pill write">Writes</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">BodyFatRecord</div><div><span class="pill write">Writes</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">BodyWaterMassRecord</div><div><span class="pill write">Writes</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">HeartRateRecord</div><div><span class="pill write">Writes*</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">StepsRecord</div><div><span class="pill read">Reads only</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">ActiveCaloriesBurnedRecord</div><div><span class="pill read">Reads only</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">TotalCaloriesBurnedRecord</div><div><span class="pill read">Reads only</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">ExerciseSessionRecord</div><div><span class="pill read">Reads only</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">DistanceRecord</div><div><span class="pill read">Reads only</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="rtype">SleepSessionRecord</div><div><span class="pill read">Reads only</span></div><div><span class="pill no">Never</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-soft);">
          * Only while continuous heart-rate monitoring is switched on, on the watch, by you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What Cairn never does</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No account or sign-in of any kind</li>
          <li>No analytics, crash reporting, or advertising SDKs</li>
          <li>No network calls &mdash; nothing is uploaded, synced to a server, or shared with a
            third party, ever</li>
          <li>No location data collected or requested</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>The phone and watch talk to each other only over Wear OS's own on-device Data Layer
            &mdash; a weigh-in on the watch and a heart-rate batch both travel exactly as far as
            your own two devices, and no further.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your controls</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Permissions</strong> can be reviewed or revoked any time in Health Connect
            (Android's own app) or in your device's app permissions settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Continuous heart rate</strong> is off by default and is switched on and off
            from the watch app's own home screen, not buried in a settings menu.</li>
          <li><strong>Deleting an entry</strong> in Cairn removes its Health Connect record with it.
            Uninstalling Cairn does not delete records already written to Health Connect &mdash;
            that data belongs to Health Connect, and you can review or clear it there directly, or
            from Health Connect's own "Data and access" screen, independent of Cairn.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>Cairn is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect data from anyone under
          13. As it collects nothing beyond your own device's Health Connect store in the first
          place, this is a description of behaviour, not a data-handling exception.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If Cairn's data handling ever changes, this page will change first, with the date above
          updated to match. Given the app's own no-network-calls design, that's expected to be rare.</p>
      </section>

      <footer>
        Questions about this policy or how Cairn handles data &mdash; <a href="mailto:clivewalkden@gmail.com">clivewalkden@gmail.com</a>
      </footer>

    </div>
  </body>
</html>
